s completely flat. One smooth complete movement cycle that fills the entire video. At 0.00 to 1.00 seconds the lantern sways gently a few centimeters back and forth on his hand, his big ears twitch once. At 1.00 to 2.00 seconds he crouches slightly, bending his knees and lowering his body about 8 centimeters, his shoulders rise, he lowers the lantern a little closer to his body as if afraid of being noticed. At 2.00 to 3.00 seconds he turns his torso slightly to the left side of the frame and turns his head to look to the left with wide frightened eyes and a tense worried expression, the ears pull back, the sack on his back shifts a little. At 3.00 to 4.00 seconds he holds the frightened look for a moment, only the lantern trembles slightly. At 4.00 to 5.00 seconds he turns his head and torso smoothly back to the front, straightens his knees and raises the lantern back to the exact starting position, the expression returns to the original sly grin. Every movement is smooth, finished to the end and unhurried, with no jerks and no stops in the middle of a movement. The pose, the lantern position, the head direction and the expression at the end of the video are identical to the first frame, so the animation repeats seamlessly. The candle flame stays small, opaque, saturated warm orange, never turns white or transparent and stays inside the lantern glass. The skin, clothing, sack, boots and lantern stay exactly as in the reference image, nothing new appears, nothing changes.\noverall_soundscape: None\nnon_diegetic_music: None", "width": ["120", 0], "height": ["120", 1], "length": ["105:107", 1], "clip": ["105:13", 0], "vae": ["105:11", 0], "first_frame": ["163", 0], "last_frame": ["163", 0]}, "class_type": "MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo", "_meta": {"title": "MiniMax H3 Image to Video", "cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.33.0"}}, "105:107": {"inputs": {"expression": "max(5, round(a * 24)) + (5 - (max(5, round(a * 24)) % 17)) % 17", "values.a": ["105:111", 0]}, "class_type": "Com